  "project_id": 7898047,
  "title": "Add an explanatory comment.",
  "description": "The reason why the frame dissector doesn't usse rec->block as the\nwtap_block_t for the record is that there might be, for example, changes\nto the record's comments that haven't yet been saved to the file, in\nwhich case we have a wtap_block_t in memory that reflects the\nmodification to the block's options.\n\n(This might be used in the future if we support editing packet *data* -\nthere was, in the GTK+ UI, an experimenal packet editor - in which case\nwe would probably keep in memory a copy of the raw record data until\nit's saved to the file.)",
